# Environment
#
# Every real secret in this repo arrives through one of these: DB_PASSWORD,
# JWT_SECRET, GEMINI_API_KEY, PAYMOB_SECRET_KEY, GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD.
# The .example templates are the documented shape and stay tracked.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!.env*.example
!*.env.example
.env.local
*.local

.vscode

# Catalog builder cache (regenerate with shop/tools/build-catalog.mjs)
shop/tools/.cache/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uploaded InstaPay receipts — NEVER COMMIT
#
# InstapayStorageService writes every uploaded receipt to
# orbitgard.instapay.uploads-dir as {yyyy}/{MM}/{uuid}.{png|jpg}. In Docker
# that is a named volume (/var/orbit/uploads, see backend/deploy/
# docker-compose.yml), which is outside the repo and therefore safe.
#
# Running the backend locally is the dangerous case: ORBIT_UPLOADS_DIR
# defaults to the relative path "uploads", so it lands next to wherever you
# started the process — usually backend/uploads/ or ./uploads/. Those files
# are real screenshots of real bank transfers, carrying account holder
# names, masked recipient names, phone numbers, amounts and bank reference
# numbers. One `git add .` after a test session publishes all of it.
uploads/
backend/uploads/
receipts/

# Local test fixtures — put throwaway receipt screenshots here
scratch/

# Test + report output
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
.angular/cache/

# Patch/merge leftovers
*.orig
*.rej
